├── drivers/                  # Out-of-tree WiFi driver packages (RTL8812AU, RTL8821CE, etc.)
├── iso/                      # ISO build directory (build/casper/, output/)
├── kernel/                   # XanMod kernel build scripts, patches (0001, 0002, 0003), cache/
├── rootfs/                   # Ubuntu 24.04 LTS root filesystem artifact
├── scripts/                  # Build automation, chroot, doctor, and boot-fix scripts
│   ├── auto-build.sh         # Main automated ISO packaging pipeline (ZSTD L19 + Level 3)
│   ├── master-doctor.sh      # Master 8-tier diagnostic and self-healing doctor
│   ├── fix-boot-display.sh   # Display manager conflict resolution & VM launcher
│   └── lib-chroot.sh         # Chroot mount/unmount library
├── tests/                    # E2E & adversarial test suite (96 total test cases)
├── .cursorrules              # Core engineering guidelines (this file)
├── AGENTS.md                 # AI agent quick reference & critical path rules
├── CHANGELOG.md              # System revision history and chronological activity log
└── README.md                 # Complete system architecture and user documentation
```

> **[CRITICAL PATH RULE]**
> The live filesystem SquashFS must always reside at `iso/build/casper/filesystem.squashfs`, never `iso/build/live/`. Casper requires this exact layout; using `live/` triggers an immediate kernel panic.

---

## 4. CRITICAL ENGINEERING RESOLUTIONS

* **[RESO_01] UNIVERSAL DRIVER STRATEGY**
  The kernel is a full-featured XanMod kernel with BORE scheduling, PREEMPT, 1000Hz timer, NTSYNC, and Kali `mac80211`/`cfg80211` wireless packet injection patches.

* **[RESO_02] CRYPTOGRAPHIC SIGNATURE BYPASS**
  Ubuntu configs enforce Canonical private keys. The build script overrides `CONFIG_SYSTEM_TRUSTED_KEYS=""` and `CONFIG_SYSTEM_REVOCATION_KEYS=""` to allow compiling without proprietary keys.

* **[RESO_03] CASPER OVERLAY REQUIREMENT**
  Debian live-boot conflicts with Ubuntu casper stack at boot. The rootfs must have casper installed and live-boot purged. The SquashFS must be at `iso/build/casper/filesystem.squashfs` with `boot=casper`.

* **[RESO_04] VM GRAPHICS FALLBACK**
  Hyper-V, VirtualBox, and QEMU without Vulkan fail on standard Wayland. The `/usr/bin/xeno-start-hyprland` script detects virtual environments using `systemd-detect-virt` and enables software rendering (`WLR_RENDERER=pixman`, `LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE=1`, `GALLIUM_DRIVER=llvmpipe`, `MESA_LOADER_DRIVER_OVERRIDE=softpipe`).

* **[RESO_05] ISO LEVEL 3 FOR OVERSIZED IMAGES**
  The rootfs exceeds 4GB. All `xorriso` invocations must specify `-iso-level 3`. GRUB volume ID must be $\le 8$ uppercase alphanumeric characters (`XENOOS`).

* **[RESO_06] DYNAMIC PATH DETECTION**
  Never hardcode `/home/xeno/Xeno-os`. Always use dynamic detection:
  `WS_DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")/.."; pwd)"`

* **[RESO_07] DUAL SERIAL & TTY1 AUTOLOGIN**
  Both `getty@tty1` and `serial-getty@ttyS0` have autologin overrides configured so both graphical desktop sessions and headless QEMU terminal testing drop directly into active user sessions.

---

## 5. MANDATORY ARCHITECTURAL GUARDRAILS

### Guardrail A: Scientific Panel Thread Isolation
Heavy math/data processing runs inside a dedicated `QObject` worker attached to a `QThread`. Worker communicates with UI strictly via `Qt.QueuedConnection` signals. Never access UI elements directly from worker threads.

### Guardrail B: Deferred VTK Viewport Loading
To prevent X11 `BadWindow` crashes on startup when placed inside a `QStackedWidget`, `threed_panel.py` must defer VTK interactor initialization until the panel becomes active (`_lazy_init_vtk()`).

### Guardrail C: Matplotlib Backend Guard
Every panel using Matplotlib must execute `matplotlib.use('Agg')` prior to importing any other Matplotlib submodules.

### Guardrail D: Scoped Realtime Security Permissions
Realtime permissions in `/etc/security/limits.d/99-hyprland.conf` are strictly scoped to `@hyprland` and `xeno` groups with `rtprio 99` and `memlock unlimited`. Global wildcards (`*`) are prohibited.

### Guardrail E: Kali APT Repository Pinning
The Kali Linux rolling repository is pinned to priority 100 in `/etc/apt/preferences.d/kali-pinning` to prevent overwriting core Ubuntu system libraries.

